---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro"
import { calculators } from "@/data/calculators"
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Health Calculators"
  description="Learn about Health Calculators: a free collection of privacy-friendly health and fitness calculators that run entirely in your browser for educational use."
>
  <article class="content">
    <p class="eyebrow">About us</p>
    <h1>About Health Calculators</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Health Calculators is a free collection of simple, transparent tools for
      estimating everyday health and fitness numbers — from Body Mass Index to
      daily calorie needs.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do</h2>
    <p>
      We build clear, fast calculators that show their working. Every tool on
      this site explains the formula it uses, walks through a worked example,
      and answers common questions, so you can understand the result rather
      than just read a number. We currently offer {calculators.length} calculators
      covering body measurements, energy expenditure, nutrition, and activity.
    </p>

    <h2>How our tools work</h2>
    <p>
      All calculations run entirely in your browser using well-established,
      publicly documented formulas such as the Mifflin-St Jeor equation for
      metabolic rate and standard MET values for activity. Nothing you type is
      sent to a server — the maths happens on your own device, instantly.
    </p>

    <h2>Our approach to accuracy</h2>
    <p>
      Health formulas are estimates, not measurements. Predictive equations are
      built from population averages and cannot account for your individual body
      composition, genetics, or medical history. We are deliberately upfront
      about these limits on every page, and we encourage you to treat results as
      a general guide rather than a precise figure.
    </p>

    <h2>Important note</h2>
    <p>
      Health Calculators does not provide medical advice. Our tools are for
      general education and information only. For any decision that affects your
      health, please consult a qualified healthcare professional. See our
      <a href="/disclaimer">health disclaimer</a> for full details.
    </p>

    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <p>
      Have a suggestion for a new calculator or spotted something that looks
      wrong? We would love to hear from you on our
      <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
